= Summary

Researcher, writer, and advocate who uses data and policy analysis to address the
economic challenges of our times. Cited in over 300 press articles, testified before
Congress four times, and made over 50 media appearances on platforms including
_CBS Sunday Morning_ and _Washington Journal_. Written work featured in
_The New York Times_ and _The Washington Post_.

= Experience

#job("Vice President of Policy and Research", "Economic Security Project", "Washington, DC", "2025–current")

- Drive strategy and goal-setting for policy, research, and agenda-setting initiatives, developing and leading efforts on affordability, housing security, and housing policy.
- Manage a policy and research team of five people plus six fellows, supporting the organization's campaigns, organizing, and advocacy at the federal and state level. Produce policy briefs, factsheets, and research projects advancing economic security policy.
- Elevate the visibility of ESP and its partners through dozens of press appearances, media citations, events, and academic discussions. Support fundraising through writing and engagement with funders.

#job("Chief Economist and Special Assistant to the President for Economic Policy", "White House National Economic Council", "Washington, DC", "2024")

- Provided ongoing economic analysis for the National Economic Advisor and support for the NEC Deputy Director on fiscal and macroeconomic policy, including inflation, growth, employment, tax, budget, and housing. Worked closely with colleagues at the Treasury Department and the Council of Economic Advisers.
- Led the formulation of the White House's messaging following all macroeconomic data releases, including themes, statements, charts, and talking points. Tracked the release process, created internal NEC measures, and directed rapid analyses of incoming indicators.
- Amplified the economic messaging of the White House and National Economic Advisor through speechwriting, content development, and media interaction. Regularly engaged external validators, experts, reporters, and academics on economic data and the President's agenda.
- Favorably adjudicated Tier 5 investigation; Top Secret/Sensitive Compartmented Information #box[(TS/SCI)] clearance granted.

#job("Director", "Roosevelt Institute", "New York, NY", "2010–2023")

- Directed the macroeconomic research team at a leading think tank, providing original research on inflation, growth, and employment. Served as a go-to expert on economic and policy issues for journalists and policymakers.
- Authored over 20 white papers and edited four comprehensive report volumes. Automated real-time data analysis with R and Python across major data releases.
- Orchestrated four multi-year research and policy initiatives on the Dodd-Frank Act, the Great Recession, economic inequality, and evolving economic paradigms. Managed teams of two internal researchers and three external fellows.
- Secured and managed research grants from the Kauffman, Ford, and Hewlett Foundations, as well as Open Philanthropy.

#job("Financial Engineer", "Moody's KMV", "San Francisco, CA", "2007–2009")

- Developed testing benchmarks for the Moody's KMV credit risk model, named 2006 "Top Provider in Trading and Banking" by _Risk Magazine_. Collaborated on five releases of RiskFrontier, developing test cases and acceptance criteria for credit risk modeling algorithms.
- Participated in discussions on approaches to credit risk modeling, focusing on the Vasicek–Kealhofer model derived from the Black–Scholes–Merton framework. Contributed to debates on capital requirements and loss reserving.
- Prototyped research algorithms in R, SAS, MATLAB, and Excel VB to replicate results. Designed a system automating collection, storage, and analysis of large data sets across four releases, cutting test execution time by 40 percent.

#job("Senior Test Engineer", "Motorola", "Schaumburg, IL", "2001–2005")

- Directed performance, load, and stress testing across four major iDEN system releases, earning a Motorola BRAVO Award for "above and beyond performance contribution." Designed automated Six Sigma-level test cases in Perl, Python, and MySQL based on models of consumer behavior. Trained six employees in testing methods.

= Education

#edu("M.S. Finance", "University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign", "2007")

- Graduate macro/microeconomics and econometrics; advanced financial research and option valuation (Monte Carlo, binomial tree) in R, SAS, and C++.

#edu("B.A. Mathematics and Computer Science", "University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign", "2001")

- Probability, statistics, data structures, graph theory, numerical methods, and nonlinear programming.

= Writing and Public Engagement

- *_Freedom From the Market_* (New Press, 2021). Named a Summer Book of 2021 in economics by the _Financial Times_; reviewed in _Democracy Journal_, _Foreign Policy_, _Foreign Affairs_, _The Wall Street Journal_, and _National Review_.
- *_Rewriting the Rules of the American Economy_* (W.W. Norton, 2015). Co-authored with Nobel laureate Joseph Stiglitz.
- Cited in over 300 articles: _The New York Times_ (32), _The Washington Post_ (23), _Vox_ (21), _Bloomberg_ (10), _Business Insider_ (9), and others. Over 25 podcast appearances and 15 television interviews.

